    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (75.69) and **Seiya Suzuki** (71.14) serving as our primary engines for production. **Corbin Carroll** is the standout play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Gausman that includes an 86% probability for stolen base opportunities due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, compounded by a strong #2 spot in the order. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** draws a highly favorable matchup against Kelly with a 5.27 xERA; our model aggressive boosts his score by 19% due to the SP skill delta and an optimal #2 lineup spot, making him a must-start despite the standard platoon considerations.\n\nWe are navigating several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, specifically for **Max Muncy** (59.65) and **Henry Bolte** (61.01). Both players benefit from projected hitting environments in the Matthews matchup, where park factors and order positioning push them into the \"Strong\" start tier. Conversely, **Zach McKinstry** (40.17) occupies the bottom of our active lineup; while he avoids the \"Below Floor\" benching threshold thanks to a favorable wind forecast, his utility is constrained by a difficult matchup against Rasmussen. Our most difficult decision was keeping **Cole Young** (33.14) on the bench. Despite his potential, the combination of a daunting matchup against Wheeler and a lower-tier batting order position resulted in a score below our 40.0 threshold, forcing us to prioritize the higher-floor efficiency of our current starters to preserve our game caps.\n\nRisks remain, particularly with **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**, who face elite arms in Gausman and Wheeler, respectively. **Josh Naylor**\u2019s score is suppressed to 48.34 due to the significant SP skill penalty, but his spot in the heart of the order keeps him active. We are monitoring **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Jose Caballero**, who remain unavailable due to injury or scheduling, leaving us with a condensed roster for today\u2019s push. As always, keep a close eye on the late-afternoon lineups for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Max Muncy** to ensure the assumed batting positions hold, as any drop in the order will require an immediate reassessment of their daily efficiency scores.",
